    "summary": "High‑energy set with soaring 'Here Comes Sunshine' and epic Truckin’>Other One",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a tight first set and a second half that rolls nonstop, highlighted by a blistering 'Truckin'' sandwich into 'The Other One' and the radiant 'Here Comes Sunshine'. Phil’s bass is massive while Jerry smokes on several tunes. Strong overall performance makes this a must‑listen for ’73 fans.",
    "review": "Seattle Center Arena on June 26, 1973 captured one of the Dead’s most kinetic summer evenings. The first set rides a smooth groove through classics like 'Casey Jones' and 'Box of Rain', but it’s the second half that truly ignites – a seamless flow from 'Bertha' into 'The Promised Land', then a thunder‑filled 'Truckin'' > Drums > The Other One sandwich that showcases Bill’s “umph” kick and Phil’s monster bass. Keith’s Rhodes bursts through on 'Playin’ In The Band' and 'He’s Gone', while Jerry’s tone is described as perfect, “smoking” across the set and even using a solo to retune without missing a beat. Highlights such as 'Here Comes Sunshine', the twin 'Other One' excursions, and an inspired 'China Cat Sunflower' → 'I Know You Rider' segue make this show a standout snapshot of the band’s 1973 peak.",
